{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI"]]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/init(_:content:)","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/init(_:id:content:)","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/init(content:)","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/init(id:content:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/body-swift.property","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/content","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/id","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/title"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"title":"Type Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/Body-swift.typealias"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Aliases"},{"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/Scene-Implementations"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"WindowGroup"}],"symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI11WindowGroupV","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"WindowGroup"}],"title":"WindowGroup","roleHeading":"Structure"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WindowGroup","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Content","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Content","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI4ViewP","text":"View","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/View","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WindowGroup"},{"type":"text","text":" as a container for a view hierarchy presented by your"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app. The hierarchy that you declare as the group’s content serves as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"template for each window that the app creates from that group:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@main","struct Mail: App {","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            MailViewer() \/\/ Declare a view hierarchy here.","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"OpenSwiftUI takes care of certain platform-specific behaviors. For example,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on platforms that support it, like macOS and iPadOS, users can open more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than one window from the group simultaneously. In macOS, users","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can gather open windows together in a tabbed interface. Also in macOS,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"window groups automatically provide commands for standard window","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"management.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every window created from the group maintains independent state. For"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"example, for each new window created from the group the system allocates new"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"storage for any "},{"code":"State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"StateObject","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" variables instantiated by the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"scene’s view hierarchy."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You typically use a window group for the main interface of an app that isn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"document-based. For document-based apps, use a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DocumentGroup"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A scene that presents a group of identically structured windows."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/windowgroup"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Scene"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/WindowGroup/id":{"url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/windowgroup\/id","role":"symbol","title":"id","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/id","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"}]},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/View":{"url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/view","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/View","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"View","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"View","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that represents part of yo